        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DIS01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Disney</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1746-09-28">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1816-12-26"/>
                    <occupation>Unitarian minister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin recorded John Disney's death on 26.12.1816 and all references up to this point are correctly coded as
referring to him. This identification can also be confirmed by looking at the radical/Unitarian context of
Godwin's meetings with Disney, which often include <persName key="HOL02">Thomas Brand Hollis</persName> (about whom Disney published a Memoir in 1808), 
  <persName key="LIN01">Theophilus Lindsey</persName> and <persName key="JEN01">Joseph Clayton Jennings</persName>.</p>
                        <p>The one later reference to Disney at a dinner at <persName key="WHI03">George White's</persName> in 1832 might be John's son, also John, who has a <title>DNB</title> entry, but 
there is no way to confirm this and as he only appears once, and there are other candidates.  Therefore, it has not been coded.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
        </body>
